SelectionEffects — Malmquist Bias: The Universe You Don't Detect
================================================

Group: Astrostatistics

Open index.html directly, or serve this directory with TeachingTools alongside
it. This is a browser-native Canvas lesson; R, Shiny and WebR are not runtime
dependencies. app.R and model.R remain unchanged as the original reference.

Model
-----
There are 2,400 galaxies at 30–800 Mpc with uniform spatial density (distance
cubed is uniform). Independent log10(L/L0) is Normal(0, 0.6^2).
M = -18 - 2.5 log10(L/L0), m = M + 5 log10(distance/Mpc) + 25.
An object is detected exactly when m <= the limiting apparent magnitude.
Nondetections stay in the parent population, even with their overlay hidden.
The orange distance-bin means omit empty bins and do not bridge their gaps;
the theoretical mean is zero, not the finite sample's exact mean.

The original controls, shallow/deep examples, guide and explanation are
retained. Animation tightens the limit from 26 to the selected 17–24 magnitude
limit in 60 cached-data steps. All distances/luminosities are fixed on playback,
resize, display changes and comparison of magnitude limits.

Intentional differences
-----------------------
Astro.createRng(seed) replaces R's generator, so identical browser seeds are
reproducible but are not bitwise-identical to set.seed(seed) in R. The full
generated luminosity range is visible rather than clipping the R plot at fixed
y-limits. Displayed counts explicitly include missing objects. There are no
cosmological, K-correction or measurement-error approximations hidden here:
these effects are excluded from the toy model and explained on the page.

Numerical API / reference checks
-------------------------------
model.js exports defaults, compute(parameters), observed(logLuminosity,
distance, limit), threshold(distance, limit), and atPhase(result, phase).
CommonJS: require("./model.js"); browser: SelectionEffectsModel.
compute returns distance, luminosity, targetLimit and a final selection
summary; atPhase returns counts, completeness, detection flags and bin means.
Expected input failures use Astro.ValidationError, including invalid pure
Node calls. Seeds are integers in [0, 2147483647].

Run from the repository root with Node 22+:
  node --test SelectionEffects/test_model.js
  TMPDIR="$PWD/SelectionEffects" node SelectionEffects/test_browser.js

The numerical tests independently check the magnitude relation and inclusive
edge, R-calibrated detection values, empty-bin/no-detection behaviour, nested
selections, count conservation and seeded stability. Browser tests check the
nondetection overlay, magnitude boundaries and cached animation, plus the
shared preset/reset/error/accessibility/mobile/file:// suite.

Runtime assets (no others)
-------------------------
index.html, model.js, app.js, ../TeachingTools/statistics.js,
../TeachingTools/browser.js, ../TeachingTools/browser.css,
../TeachingTools/lesson.js.
